    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105284" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρί-στομος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>three-edged</i> or
				<i>three-pointed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰχμή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.167
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. δόρυ,</span> of the trident,
				<i><span class="en">
				Max.Tyr.
				10.8
			</span></i>; <i>with three mouths,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ῥοδανός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					4.1.8
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίστομον, τό,</span> dub. sens., prob. place-name, in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PTeb.</u>
				112.2
			</span></i>, al. (<span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>, cf. ii <i><span class="en">
				p.405
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιτολόγοι Τριστόμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ostr.</u>
					1097
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1072 iii 2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>, etc.</div>
